window.EN={"1":"Having saved the village of Nabata, Roy and the others pass through the desert guided by Igrene","2":"and finally set out for the Etrurian homeland to defeat the coup faction.","3":"But word reached him there — terrible news from the elder of the village of Nabata.","4":"The dragon girl Fae had vanished from the village of Nabata, chasing after Roy and the others.","5":"If Fae should fall into the hands of the coup faction — and Bern lurking behind them — it would be a disaster.","6":"Roy and the others traced Fae's whereabouts","7":"and headed for a small fort near the Etrurian border.","8":"(Soldier): General Raith.","9":"(Soldier): It's about that strange girl we caught earlier.","10":"(Raith): The girl? ...Ah, the one who was said to be loitering around the castle.","11":"(Raith): What, you're still dealing with that thing?","12":"(Raith): Just throw her out of the castle already!","13":"(Soldier): W-well, the thing is, that girl had this on her...","14":"(Raith): Hm? ...Is this a Dragonstone?","15":"(Soldier): ...I thought so too, which is why I came to report it.","16":"(Raith): You've seen a Dragonstone before?","17":"(Soldier): Yes, during the invasion of Lycia...","18":"(Soldier): \"Dragons\" always carried one when in human form.","19":"(Raith): ...But it feels a little different from the ones they had.","20":"(Raith): Either way, this concerns the \"dragons.\"","21":"(Raith): It would be best to report to His Majesty Zephiel and receive instructions.","22":"(Raith): Make sure that girl doesn't escape the castle! Keep close watch!","23":"*Only if Perceval was not recruited in Chapter 13","24":"(Douglas): Percival, there's no need to push yourself.","25":"(Perceval): Lord Douglas, please don't worry about me. Please return to King Mordred's side.","26":"(Douglas): Putting down the Lycian Alliance army","27":"(Douglas): isn't work that calls for a \"Knight-General\" to show up in person.","28":"(Douglas): Leaving it entirely to you... that cunning Roartz.","29":"(Perceval): I imagine he's wary of my betraying him.","30":"(Perceval): If I stay in the royal capital, who knows when my throat might be slit, he must think.","31":"(Douglas): That man, wary of betrayal from his own kin? Ha! Don't make me laugh.","32":"(Douglas): That man was the first to betray his loyalty to His Majesty!","33":"(Perceval): Lord Douglas, there is no one whose loyalty runs as deep as yours.","34":"(Douglas): If we're saying that, Percival, you're no different.","35":"(Perceval): ...When Prince Myrddin was still alive, I never once wavered.","36":"(Perceval): I believed I would serve the Kingdom of Etruria for life and never lose sight of my loyalty.","37":"(Perceval): To fulfill my duty for His Majesty's life... that alone should be reason enough to fight, and yet—","38":"(Douglas): Are you having doubts?","39":"(Perceval): A little.","40":"(Perceval): But it's no problem. Nothing changes because of it.","41":"(Douglas): I see...","42":"(Douglas): Percival, from here on, this is just me talking to myself. Even if you can hear me, don't answer.","43":"(Perceval): ......","44":"(Douglas): Etruria, you see...","45":"(Douglas): will perish along with His Majesty, without waiting for this war to end...","46":"(Perceval): ! Lord Douglas!?","47":"(Douglas): Listen!","48":"(Douglas): No matter what happens, I will remain by His Majesty's side until my final day.","49":"(Douglas): No matter what happens.","50":"(Douglas): But Percival, you are different. You're the man who must carry the next Etruria on his shoulders.","51":"(Douglas): I can't say it now, but someday, without fail, a day will come when glory returns to Etruria.","52":"(Douglas): So leave Etruria soon, and wait for your time.","53":"(Perceval): Lord Douglas! Just what do you—","54":"(Soldier): General Percival, sir! We've spotted the Lycian Alliance army ahead!","55":"(Soldier): Your orders!!","56":"(Douglas): Go. I'll return to Aquleia as well.","57":"(Perceval): ...After the Lycian Alliance army! Forward!!","58":"(Roy): That dragon girl named Fae, is that castle where she was taken?","59":"(Marinus): Yes, people from around here say they saw it happen.","60":"(Igrene): Sir Roy, I'm sorry for the trouble our village's people have caused...","61":"(Igrene): My apologies, even though you're hurrying along the road to the royal capital Aquleia.","62":"(Roy): No, it would be a disaster if that girl fell into enemy hands.","63":"(Igrene): As long as the Dragonstone isn't found, I think she should be safe while in human form.","64":"(Roy): What exactly is this \"Dragonstone\"?","65":"(Igrene): While in human form,","66":"(Igrene): it's a stone that seals away a \"dragon's\" true power.","67":"(Igrene): To maintain a \"dragon's\" true form in this world apparently requires a tremendous amount of power.","68":"(Igrene): Normally, by taking \"human\" form, the loss of power is kept to a minimum.","69":"(Roy): I wonder if the \"one who is not human\" took human form for the same reason.","70":"(Igrene): From what you told me the other day, I'd guess that's likely so.","71":"(Igrene): Apparently, it was after the \"War of Dragons and Men\" that \"dragons\" started taking human form.","72":"(Roy): From that long ago...","73":"(Igrene): Yes.","74":"(Marinus): Sir Roy.","75":"(Marinus): The one I sent to scout the castle has returned.","76":"(Roy): How did it go?","77":"(Marinus): Well, it seems quite a number of soldiers came out from the castle just now.","78":"(Marinus): They appear to be heightening their guard.","79":"(Roy): I see... if that's so, they may have found out she's a \"dragon.\"","80":"(Marinus): And to make matters worse, it seems the army guarding the border has noticed us.","81":"(Roy): We need to rescue that girl quickly.","82":"(Garret): So this is going to be a battlefield too, huh...","83":"(Bandit): So, what do we do, Boss Garret!","84":"(Garret): The army's lot is going to take it anyway.","85":"(Garret): So there's no harm in us taking it for ourselves.","86":"(Garret): Let's go ahead and clean out the treasures from the villages around here.","87":"(Bandit): Yes, sir!","88":"(Garret): But don't you go killing anyone you don't need to.","89":"(Bandit): Yes, sir...","90":"(Bandit): You're too soft, really.","91":"(Bandit): Well, if it comes to it, we can just blame the army's lot.","92":"(Soldier): Lord Raith, the reinforcements are ready!","93":"(Raith): Good, tell them to deploy in order.","94":"(Soldier): Yes, sir.","95":"(Larum): Lord Perceval~! It's Lord Perceval, right~?","96":"(Larum): Oh good, I've been looking for you~ I'm, you see~...","97":"(Larum): Wah, hey! Wait a second!! Stop your horse and listen to me!","98":"(Perceval): ...Who are you?","99":"(Larum): Shocked... We should've met a few times already!","100":"(Perceval): ...I feel like I saw you at Lord Douglas's mansion.","101":"(Larum): Yes! That's it! See, you do know me after all!","102":"(Perceval): The one I saw there was a bit more... ordinary-looking girl.","103":"(Larum): What? What's that supposed to mean!?","104":"(Larum): Well, never mind that, more importantly—","105":"(Larum): I'm Larum! I've come on an errand from Prince Myrddin!","106":"(Perceval): Prince... Myrddin, you say?","107":"(Perceval): Don't talk nonsense. The prince died in an accident a year ago.","108":"(Larum): Heh heh heh...","109":"(Larum): Ta-dah! Doesn't this crest catch your eye?","110":"(Perceval): !! That's... the prince's...!","111":"(Larum): Heh, seems I've impressed you.","112":"(Larum): Then look at this letter too! The prince wrote it for you, Lord Perceval!","113":"(Perceval): ...... ...... ......","114":"(Perceval): This is certainly... the prince's handwriting.","115":"(Perceval): I see... so he was alive after all... Then there's no need to hesitate any longer!","116":"(Perceval): If the prince is with the Lycian Alliance, then there's only one path for me to take.","117":"(Larum): Eh? Already?","118":"(Larum): Mmm... I had so much more prepared for this~","119":"(Larum): I was planning to say something dramatic like \"If you'll still fight, then cut me down instead!\"~","120":"(Roy): General Perceval!","121":"(Perceval): General Roy.","122":"(Perceval): Allow me to lend you my strength as well.","123":"(Perceval): Would that be all right?","124":"(Roy): Of course!","125":"(Roy): To have someone of General Perceval's caliber join our side—","126":"(Roy): there's nothing more reassuring than that. But why the sudden change of heart?","127":"(Perceval): ...Must I give a reason?","128":"(Roy): No, if there are circumstances you can't speak of, I won't force it out of you.","129":"(Perceval): I'm sorry... When the time comes, I'll tell you.","130":"(Lilina): Wait!","131":"(Garret): What's this, who are you?","132":"(Lilina): Why? Why do you people attack villages like this?","133":"(Garret): Huh? What, who are you?","134":"(Lilina): Please, tell me the reason you attack villages!","135":"(Garret): A reason... a reason, huh.","136":"(Garret): Well, if I had to say, maybe it's your fault.","137":"(Lilina): Our... fault?","138":"(Garret): That's right. Thanks to you lot running your war,","139":"(Garret): more and more people like us, who can't eat without stealing, keep piling up.","140":"(Lilina): We're fighting in order to help people like that.","141":"(Garret): Heh, heh. Everyone says that, all in chorus.","142":"(Garret): But what's the reality? All talk, and nothing you actually do for us.","143":"(Garret): In the end, you lot just can't see the people who get trampled underfoot.","144":"(Garret): So, once you understand that, hurry up and get out of the way.","145":"(Lilina): ...I won't.","146":"(Garret): What did you say!? Hey, you'd better quit it before—","147":"(Lilina): I'm not moving from here.","148":"(Lilina): If you want to attack, go ahead and do as you please...","149":"(Garret): Wha...","150":"(Lilina): If I move from here now... I'll become one of those people who are nothing but empty talk, just like you say.","151":"(Lilina): But I'm telling the truth! We really are fighting to save people!","152":"(Garret): You...","153":"(Garret): ...Heh heh. To think there's someone these days who seriously believes such a pointless thing.","154":"(Lilina): Pointless... is it?","155":"(Lilina): Our... feelings...","156":"(Garret): Still, you know, it's not bad, that kind of thing.","157":"(Lilina): ! Ah... then—","158":"(Garret): ...You win. I lose to you.","159":"(Garret): Since I've lost, let me fight alongside you too.","160":"(Garret): Let's see this \"truth\" you're talking about.","161":"(Lilina): Thank you.","162":"(Lilina): It'll be fine. If we keep fighting together, I believe people will come to understand, surely.","163":"(Garret): Heh, quite the confidence you've got there.","164":"(Garret): Name's Garret. Anyway, nice to meet ya... uh, what was it again?","165":"(Lilina): Lilina.","166":"(Garret): Nice to meet you, Lilina.","167":"(Civilian): That little one who was wandering around in front of our house...","168":"(Civilian): Poor thing, she got taken off to the castle.","169":"(Civilian): Here, I'll give you this, so won't you do something about it for us?","170":"(Civilian): It's a book the priest who used to live in our village treasured.","171":"(Civilian): That priest too... got caught by the people at the castle, and never came back after that.","172":"(Civilian): This is Mahamane's Rod, a rod that repairs your belongings.","173":"(Civilian): It restores any weapon, tome, or rod to brand new condition.","174":"(Civilian): But there's just one thing it can't fix, you know what that is?","175":"(Civilian): That's right, this rod itself.","176":"(Civilian): It repairs everything... while it alone just withers away.","177":"(Elder): Rumor has it that the Three Generals of Etruria have scattered to the winds, I heard...","178":"(Elder): The hearts of us common folk too have become completely shattered.","179":"(Elder): I just hope it doesn't come to the same Three Generals fighting one another...","180":"(Civilian): Lately, it seems bandits have been showing up around here.","181":"(Civilian): It's dangerous, isn't it... surely some heartless, merciless fellow.","182":"Hm, I don't understand this... why attack this castle now?","183":"There's something going on here, isn't there? Something...","184":"I thought as much... that girl... she isn't human, is she.","185":"Her goal is the same as ours... to make use of the dragon... I'd wager.","186":"(Marinus): Sir Roy, I found the dragon girl!","187":"(Elder): You found her! I'm coming now!","188":"(Marinus): There now, girl, won't you greet Sir Roy properly?","189":"(Fae): Sniff, sniff...","190":"(Roy): It's all right, Marinus.","191":"(Roy): ...Why did you go and follow us off on your own like that?","192":"(Fae): Because... I wanted to see outside, that's why...","193":"(Marinus): What did you say!? Just for that reason...","194":"(Marinus): Do you have any idea how much of an uproar this caused!","195":"(Fae): But, but","196":"(Fae): Fae was never, ever, ever let outside!","197":"(Fae): ...I wasn't supposed to be seen by people's eyes, and I was always, always","198":"(Fae): always in a dark room, that's why...","199":"(Roy): ......","200":"(Marinus): Sir Roy, what will you do?","201":"(Roy): ...You must have had it rough too, huh. But still,","202":"(Roy): because of that, you caused trouble for the village elder and a lot of other people, you understand that, right?","203":"(Fae): I-I'm sorry...","204":"(Roy): Do you really regret it?","205":"(Fae): Yeah.","206":"(Roy): Then from here on, you can come along with us if you want.","207":"(Fae): Eh! Really?","208":"(Marinus): ...Are you sure?","209":"(Roy): There's a chance the enemy has already learned this child exists.","210":"(Roy): Rather than send her back as she is, it'd be better to keep her where we can watch over her.","211":"(Fae): Yay, yay!","212":"(Marinus): Now don't you go getting carried away!","213":"(Roy): But you can't go wandering off on your own anymore, understand?","214":"(Fae): Okay! Fae promises!","215":"*Only if the entire Knight-General unit of NPCs survives","216":"(Soldier): General Perceval.","217":"(Soldier): Until further orders, we will stand by at this castle and prepare for an attack from the coup faction.","218":"(Perceval): I'm counting on you.","219":"(Soldier): This is treasure we found within the castle. Please, take it.","220":"(Soldier): Then, General... regarding Etruria... please, we beg you.","221":"(Perceval): I understand. Leave it to me.","222":"(Soldier): Yes, sir!"};
